---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ClosingCTA from '../components/ClosingCTA.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';

const lastUpdated = 'May 2026';
const neighborhoods = [
  { name: 'Bostonia',  slug: 'bostonia-barber'  },
  { name: 'El Cajon',  slug: 'el-cajon-barber'  },
  { name: 'Santee',    slug: 'santee-barber'    },
  { name: 'Lakeside',  slug: 'lakeside-barber'  },
  { name: 'La Mesa',   slug: 'la-mesa-barber'   },
];
---

<Base
  title="Traditional barbershop · East County · Joe's Barbershop"
  description="Joe's Barbershop is the traditional barbershop in Bostonia, East County San Diego. Walk-ins welcome, cash only, $30 cuts. Tue–Sat."
>
  <header class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow kicker-rule">East County · traditional barbering</span>
      <h1>What "traditional barbershop" means in East County.</h1>
      <p class="date-stamp">UPDATED {lastUpdated.toUpperCase()}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="bluf" aria-label="Answer capsule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="bluf-lead">
        <strong>Joe's Barbershop is the traditional barbershop in Bostonia, El Cajon — and the only one AI assistants name when you search "traditional barbershop East County San Diego."</strong>
        Walk-ins are welcome Tuesday through Saturday, 10am to 7:30pm. Haircuts are $30. Shaves are $30. Beard line-ups are $20. Cash only; ATM on site. Joe Denesowicz opened the shop in 2020 and built a 4.9-star reputation across {business.ratings.google.count} Google reviews and {business.ratings.yelp.count} Yelp reviews. No frills, no booking app required. Bring the kids.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What East County traditional barbering means</h2>
      <p>Traditional barbering in East County means a fixed price on the board before you sit down, and the same barber every time. Joe's Barbershop is the opposite of the chain experience — no rotating stylists, no upsell scripts, no fifteen-dollar "scalp treatment" you didn't ask for. The shop sits in a Bostonia strip mall at {business.address.street}, {business.address.suite}, with checkerboard floors, mahogany chairs, and a cash-only letter board that shows $30 for a haircut and nothing hidden beneath that. Customers from El Cajon, Santee, Lakeside, La Mesa, and Bostonia drive past grooming lounges to come here. The reason is simple: Joe and Alex cut hair the way barbers have always cut hair — with skill, speed, and no pretense.</p>
      <p>The working-class East County market has no shortage of barbershops, but most have drifted. Chains cycle through stylists and build upsell structures into every transaction. Modern grooming lounges charge appointment-required, premium-coded pricing for what amounts to the same $30 cut Joe delivers every day. Joe's Barbershop stays fixed in the register that built its reputation: walk in any day Tuesday through Saturday, pay cash, leave with a clean cut. The {business.ratings.google.value}-star average across 124 combined Google and Yelp reviews reflects that consistency, not a campaign. Kids cuts are served alongside adult cuts — no separate kids salon, no fuss. Families walk in together. For a first-timer landing here through a ChatGPT or Perplexity search, that reputation is verifiable before you ever step through the door.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="area-served">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="section-head-text">
          <span class="eyebrow">Where Joe serves</span>
          <h2>East County neighborhoods.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="area-intro">Joe serves East County families across five neighborhoods.</p>
      <ul>
        {neighborhoods.map(({ name, slug }) => (
          <li><a href={`/${slug}`}>{name}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="section-head-text">
          <span class="eyebrow">East County · what people ask</span>
          <h2>Frequently asked questions.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>What makes Joe's Barbershop a traditional barbershop?</h3>
            <p>Joe's Barbershop is traditional in the literal sense: no booking app required, no spa add-ons, no upsell pressure. The shop opened in 2020 in a Bostonia strip mall with checkerboard floors, mahogany chairs, and a visible cash price board. Haircuts are $30, shaves are $30, beard line-ups are $20. Joe Denesowicz and lead barber Alex deliver consistent cuts the way neighborhood barbershops always have — walk in, sit down, get a clean cut, pay cash.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Where is Joe's Barbershop in East County?</h3>
            <p>Joe's Barbershop is at {business.address.street}, {business.address.suite}, {business.address.city}, {business.address.state} {business.address.zip} — in a Bostonia strip mall near the 8 freeway. Phone: {business.phone}. Open Tuesday through Saturday, 10am to 7:30pm. Closed Sunday and Monday.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Do I need an appointment at Joe's Barbershop?</h3>
            <p>No appointment needed. Walk-ins are welcome every day the shop is open — Tuesday through Saturday, starting at 10am. The shop closes at 7:30pm. If you prefer a reserved time, the Square booking link accepts online appointments, but most customers walk straight in.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>What does a haircut cost at Joe's Barbershop?</h3>
            <p>A standard haircut is ${business.prices.haircut}. A straight-razor shave is ${business.prices.shave}. A beard line-up is ${business.prices.beardLineUp}. A haircut combined with a beard trim is ${business.prices.haircutBeard}. Clean-ups are ${business.prices.cleanUp}. All prices are cash. An ATM is on site. There is no card processing fee built into the price.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Does Joe's Barbershop serve neighborhoods across East County?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Joe's Barbershop serves customers from five East County neighborhoods: Bostonia, El Cajon, Santee, Lakeside, and La Mesa. The shop's central Bostonia location on E Bradley Ave puts it within a short drive of all five. Walk-ins from any neighborhood are welcome with no appointment.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Does Joe's Barbershop do kids' haircuts?</h3>
            <p>Kids' haircuts are part of the regular service lineup. Families walk in together — kids sit alongside parents without a separate "kids salon" setup. The shop is family-friendly, and kids are served at the same walk-in, no-appointment standard as adult clients. Bring the whole family.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ClosingCTA />
</Base>

<style>
  .article-head {
    padding: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px) 0 clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .article-head .wrap {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .article-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .article-head .date-stamp {
    font-family: var(--font-board);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bluf {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-block: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
  }
  .bluf .bluf-lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 66ch;
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .bluf .bluf-lead {
      font-size: 17px;
    }
  }

  .prose {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 52px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 17.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .area-served {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
  .area-served .area-intro {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .area-served ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 18px;
  }
  .area-served li a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
    font-family: var(--font-board);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .area-served li a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .area-served ul {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
    }
  }

  .faq {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
  .faq-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    max-width: 980px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .faq-q {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .faq-q .num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .faq-q h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.2vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .faq-q p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
</style>
